# PHP

Target supported PHP versions with strict typing and clear boundaries.

## Required behavior

- Use `declare(strict_types=1);` in new PHP files.
- Prefer typed properties, parameters, and return types.
- Avoid suppressing type errors to “make it work.”

## Anti-patterns

- Mixing Laravel Eloquent / Artisan mental models into PHP application code.
- Untyped public APIs in new code.
